                  <zone forceUpdate='true' h='5867' id='34' type-v2='text' w='89441' x='476' y='11133'>
                    <formatted-text>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='8' italic='true' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Executive Market Insights: </run>
                      <run lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='8' italic='true' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Electrification Parity:</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='8' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'> All 3 Indian EV models (</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='8' italic='true' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Nexon EV, XUV400, ZS EV</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='8' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>) achieve 455–465 km certified range across a ₹16.7L – ₹21.8L price bracket, establishing a high value-per-km frontier. </run>
                      <run lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='8' italic='true' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>BNCAP 5-Star Benchmark:</run>
                      <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='8' italic='true' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Æ </run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='8' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>6 airbags and 5-star crash safety are now standardized across flagship Sedans and SUVs (</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='8' italic='true' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Nexon, Scorpio N, Verna, City</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='8' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>). </run>
                      <run lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='8' lmargin='600' rmargin='600'>Efficiency Continuum: Two-wheelers dominate urban transit with 48–66 kmpl efficiency, while commercial hauliers deliver up to 1,750 Nm torque.</run>
                    </formatted-text>
                    <zone-style>
